- Pass current date into ProblemFinder, then have it use that to see what year to assume
    It probably makes sense to say the "closest" date? Like if they say "Jan 1" and it's Feb 1, 2026, assume they mean 2026, but if it's Dec 1 2026, assume they mean 2027.
- Handle the situation where the user is *going to specify* the year
    This might be tough, but if I say "Sat Jan 1, 2000" that shouldn't be wrong even if Jan 1 is a Sun "this year".
